=== implementation ===
paths:
- packages/architecture-enforcement/src/analyzer.ts
- packages/architecture-enforcement/src/pin-refresh-checkpoint.ts (new)
- packages/architecture-enforcement/src/v2-manifest-validation.ts
- packages/architecture-enforcement/src/architecture-pin-refresh-cli.ts
- docs/architecture-enforcement.md

The prelude stays global at analyzer.ts. The module loop is one exported
function, analyzeArchitectureModuleFindings. assembleArchitectureAnalysis keeps
the old key order and sort. ArchitectureAnalysisStopped carries modulesDone and
modulesTotal. The store holds version, headCommit, candidatePaths, sourcePaths,
and two pass records of module findings. The store holds no hash and no
checksum. Its identity is the Git commit only. The store write uses a temporary
file, then a rename. Exit code 3 means partial with progress.

Design note for the reviewers. Two points need the review.
1. The resumable evidence function takes analyzeSources from the CLI. The CLI
   imports the exported analyzeArchitectureSources and passes it. Reason: the
   cost file wraps the exported function, so the AC-7 and AC-15 seams count each
   pass. The resume file needs the same count.
2. A resumed run that finishes both passes stores its last batch, then exits 3
   and leaves the complete store. The next run combines the store, writes the
   manifest, and deletes the store. Reason: AC-10, AC-13, and AC-16 read a store
   snapshot after an exit 3 run, so the snapshot must hold both complete passes
   before the manifest write. A run that starts with no store and finishes both
   passes in one run still writes at once, so the FR-4 and FR-7 one-run path
   keeps its counts.

